@module tables ; Tables: room build, title scene, gates, actor scripts
$7300 b RoomPatternStarts 16 ; The low bytes in page $73 of the 16 room patterns, indexed by a room record's low nibble
> The room builder at $9F63 takes the low nibble of a room-stream byte, reads H = $73, L = RoomPatternStarts[n] ($9F7D-$9F80) and walks the pattern from $73xx (RoomPatterns). Values $10-$41: the patterns lie at $7310-$7344.
> Witness: $7300-$7306 read by $9F63 in deaths and rooms (L1 byte profiles).
@res rooms/outline-starts.bin
$7310 b RoomPatterns 8 ; Room patterns read by $9F63: a byte a cell step, bit 7 two tiles, bit 6 back to the row start, bits 0-5 the step
> Read through DE = $73xx by the loop $9F96: bit 7 set puts two tiles ($A408 twice), bits 0-5 are added to the tile-map offset, bit 6 restarts the column from $6BDE. Patterns 0-8 here ($7310-$7329); the rest go on at RoomPatternsMore past the two variables.
> Witness: $7300-$731D, $7322-$7329 read by $9F63 (deaths, rooms).
@res rooms/outlines-1.bin
$732A b DrawColumnPos 1 ; Two words of drawing state: the column position (a word) and the row position (a word)
> $8F75 writes BC from $8FDD (the actor's X, +$22 applied) to $732A and BC from $9000 (Y - +$21) to $732C; the cell writer CellScreenAddress $8803 writes the cell column x 4 to $732A. Readers: SpriteScreenAddress $8828, ComposeActorCells $8907, $8A90, $8C68, $8CE5, $9A27, $8F3B (bit 0 of $732C picks the composer buffer $5D4A / $5D42).
> Witness: read and written in every recording (c1, deaths, menu ...).
$732C DrawRowPos ; the row position (a word), from $9000
$732E b RoomPatternsMore 8 ; Room patterns 9-15 read by $9F63 (continued from RoomPatterns)
> Witness: $732E, $7333-$7344 read by $9F63 (rooms).
@res rooms/outlines-2.bin
$7345 b RoomShapes 2 ; Tile shapes for $A02E: (tile, step) pairs, a step with bit 7 set ends the shape
> PutShape $A02E: DE = $73xx (E from the room stream, $A01F), (DE) is a tile code stored at (HL), the next byte is added to L; a step of $80 or more ends. The room code handlers 0-3 ($A016) place them.
> Witness: $7345-$7394 read by $A02E in c1, menu, gameover, deaths, rooms.
@res rooms/strings.bin
$73BD b ShapeTilesA 4 ; Four tile codes read through IX by $A357 when the room byte's high nibble is 2
> $A357: IX = $73BD when (BC-1) AND $F0 = $20, else ShapeTilesB $73C1. Witness: $73BD-$73C0 read by $A357 (rooms).
$73C1 ShapeTilesB ; the other four tile codes for $A357
@res rooms/decor-tiles.bin
$73C5 b SpecialTiles 2 ; Two tile codes ($55, $54) searched with CPIR by $9CB1
> $9CB1: the tile under the actor at $6A00 + B is looked up in these two bytes. Witness: read by $9CA1 / $9CA7 / $9CB1 in c1, menu, opt2-4, rooms.
@res rooms/ladder-tiles.bin
$73C7 w RoomCodeHandlers 1 ; The room-stream code handlers, 15 addresses ($9FFF: index = the code x 2)
> $9FEF / $9FFF: HL = $73C7, A = the code ($0D or less), RLCA, $A00F adds and jumps (JP (HL)). Codes 0-3 $A016 (shapes), 4 $A039 (the room's strip), 5 $A0B9, 6 $A0C4, 7 $A0D2, 8 $A0D6, 9 $A0C9, 10 $A0BE, 11 $A006, 12 $A0E2, 13 $A1F1, 14 $A357.
> Witness: $73CD-$73E6 read by $9FEF / $A00F (c1, gameover, menu, opt2-4, deaths, rooms).
$73E5 w ActorKindHandlers 1 ; Ten handler addresses read from DE = $73E5 by $9A99
> $72DE, $921C, $9238, $91EE, $91E1, $91F4, $920A, $9215, $91A9, $91D4. Witness: $73E7-$73F8 read by $9A99 (every play recording).
$73F9 s Spare73F9 ; Seven zero bytes, read by no recording
@res leftovers/spare-73f9.bin
$7400 b StructureRecords 6 ; Six-byte structure records: +0 the first tile (bit 7 a flag), +1-+5 the next tiles
> $A0EE: IX = base + 6 x (the high nibble of the room byte) ($8EDD multiplies), the bases $7400 ($A0C4), $7436 ($A0C9), $7496 ($A0E2), StructureSetD $7511 ($A0BE), $7571 ($A0D8), $75AD ($A0B9). $A101 / $A109 / $A416 put (IX+0) AND $7F, (IX+2), (IX+3) ... into the tile map.
> The record at $74BA (set C, record 6) is two variables: ComposeDest.
> Witness: $7436-$74AC read by $A0CD / $A109 / $A416 (deaths, rooms); $7400-$7435 read by no recording (handler 6 $A0C4 did not run).
$7436 StructureSetB ; base $A0C9 (room code 9)
$7496 StructureSetC ; base $A0E4 (room code 12)
$74BA ComposeDest ; a word: the composer's buffer, $5D4A or $5D42, written by $8F3B, read by ComposeActorCells $8907
$74C0 ; set C goes on
